From: ub548117c8aed3bfb at groups.google.com (Chris Brown)
Date: Mon, 14 Nov 2016 23:53:01 +0000
Subject: General guidelines for building a mesh?
Message-ID: <b3uinntrh9E.LjW6-yDhAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/b3uinntrh9E/m/LjW6-yDhAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,
 Can anyone point me to some general guidelines for building a mesh for spatially continous models, such as a linear model with a Matern covariance effect?
I was wondering how the minimum edge size of triangles ('cutoff'), maximum size and buffer around the points will affect inferences about model parameters.
Thanks,
Chris

From uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com  Tue Nov 15 02:29:06 2016
From: uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com (Finn Lindgren)
