Dear INLA developers,

In the paper "Bayesian estimation for generalised linear mixed models" (Fong et al, 2010), it is written that "There is an urgent need for diagnosis tools to flag when INLA is inaccurate."

Is there any such tools implemented to r-inla, yet?

Or what are your suggestions to be sure about the accuracy of INLA results (without comparing to MCMC results)? For example, comparing "simplified.laplace" and "laplace" results can be sufficient?

Thank you very much for your help,

Best,

Burak Kursad Gunhan

